    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Greystones is delighted to present No. 64 Glenview Park to the market. This charming home offers an excellent opportunity for discerning purchasers seeking a property with future potential, whether through extending the existing accommodation or adding a garden cabin. No. 64 is further enhanced by a superb rear garden measuring approximately 24m in length, enjoying a sunny westerly orientation. Beautifully presented following a comprehensive remodel in 2021, the property is in true turnkey condition and will appeal equally to first-time buyers and those looking to downsize in comfort and style.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance porch with sliding patio door, leading to a welcoming entrance hall. Stylish grey laminate flooring begins in the hall and continues seamlessly throughout the home. A cleverly designed storage area provides ample space for golf clubs and additional household items. The living room, positioned to the front, enjoys an abundance of natural light through a large window and features an open fireplace, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere. Off the inner hallway lies a fully refurbished shower room, complete with a low-profile shower tray, contemporary wall and floor tiling, modern sanitary ware, and a lighted mirror. Two Velux roof lights flood the space with natural light. To the rear, the redesigned kitchen is both practical and attractive, featuring quality Bosch appliances, ample cabinetry, and stylish wall tiling. French patio doors open directly onto the sunny rear garden. The inner hall also provides access to three well-proportioned bedrooms.\n\nTo the front, the property is complemented by a well-maintained garden with a variety of plants and shrubs, creating strong kerb appeal. Off-street parking is provided, and an extra-wide side entrance leads to the impressive rear garden. This tiered outdoor space extends to approximately 24m and includes a patio area off the kitchen, three lawned sections, and a selection of mature fruit trees to the rear. A charming wildflower area adds a natural, meadow-like feel, while also providing a peaceful and private setting.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality of the interior and the exceptional outdoor space this fine home has to offer.\n\n3 Bed semi-detached bungalow\nAccommodation of approx. 58 Sq M\nSuperb westerly facing garden of approx. 24m in length\nRemodelled interior (2021)\nRewired (2021)\nNew kitchen with Bosch appliances (2021)\nNew shower room (2021)\nNew oil-fired central heating system and radiators (2021)\nAttractive grey oak laminate flooring throughout\nDouble glazed windows throughout\nFrench patio doors replaced (2021)\nOff-street parking\nEasy access to and from the N11\n4.9km to Newtownmountkennedy\n5.7km to Kilcoole\n3.7km to Delgany\n6.8km to Greystones DART Station\nShort stroll to L1 bus stop serving Greystones and Bray\nShort stroll to 133 bus stop serving Dublin City"
      },
